abstract: >-
  LaTeX source of a submitted manuscript on pulsatile blood flow in viscoelastic vessels, with the Maple worksheets and
  the SymPy scripts that support it. From the axisymmetric Euler equations of an ideal fluid in a Kelvin–Voigt vessel,
  the manuscript derives the cylindrical Serre–Green–Naghdi and Boussinesq equations and the Korteweg–de Vries and
  Benjamin–Bona–Mahony reductions, and studies their dispersion relations, solitary waves, conservation laws, point
  symmetries and modulational instability; the scripts verify its algebra symbolically.
